WEBVTT

00:00:02.770 --> 00:00:03.940
Sayu!

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:11.020
Where the hell have you been?

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:15.700
People were spreading all these
weird rumors because of you!

00:00:16.060 --> 00:00:17.610
M-Mom!

00:00:17.610 --> 00:00:19.700
We've got a guest. That's enough.

00:00:23.860 --> 00:00:27.200
This is Yoshida-san. 
He took care of her for a long time.

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:29.780
I asked him to come with me.

00:00:32.370 --> 00:00:34.410
"Took care of her," huh?

00:02:22.120 --> 00:02:27.120
"Mother"

00:02:22.270 --> 00:02:23.400
Sayu...

00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:26.740
I'm fine. Let's go.

00:02:27.760 --> 00:02:29.080
Come in.

00:02:29.550 --> 00:02:30.670
Right this way.

00:02:32.480 --> 00:02:33.460
All right.

00:02:56.180 --> 00:03:00.400
So? What did you expect to accomplish?

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:04.940
Running away from home for so long. 
Causing problems for your family.

00:03:04.940 --> 00:03:08.250
You caused no end of problems 
when you lived here, but this was worse.

00:03:12.320 --> 00:03:15.480
I don't understand what you want to do.

00:03:17.720 --> 00:03:19.050
...not even trying.

00:03:20.230 --> 00:03:21.300
What?

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:23.760
You're not even trying to understand.

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:27.820
Well, I don't know what you're thinking.

00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:30.730
You don't say anything.

00:03:31.150 --> 00:03:36.290
Do you remember what
I said to you the day I left?

00:03:36.290 --> 00:03:39.820
What was it, again? I forget.

00:03:41.390 --> 00:03:42.920
I knew it.

00:03:43.530 --> 00:03:47.400
You don't care about me.

00:03:47.810 --> 00:03:50.750
You don't even try to understand me.

00:03:51.160 --> 00:03:55.400
You've been home for five minutes, 
and already you're complaining.

00:03:55.400 --> 00:03:58.970
Did you run away just because 
you wanted to spite your family?

00:03:58.970 --> 00:04:00.010
No!

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:03.090
I...

00:04:04.680 --> 00:04:08.740
I just... wanted to get away from you.

00:04:09.970 --> 00:04:13.290
From the mother who didn't even try 
to understand me.

00:04:14.880 --> 00:04:19.780
From the mother who told me

00:04:21.430 --> 00:04:24.320
that she thought I killed my only friend!

00:04:26.720 --> 00:04:30.760
So what did you think 
running away would accomplish?

00:04:30.760 --> 00:04:35.080
Even if you left, there was nothing
you could have done on your own.

00:04:35.940 --> 00:04:37.180
Well...

00:04:39.550 --> 00:04:43.450
<i>Still, it was her only choice.</i>

00:04:43.860 --> 00:04:50.790
<i>And it was her mom who made it 
so that it was her only choice.</i>

00:04:51.460 --> 00:04:56.700
And then you end up staying 
at the house of a strange man.

00:04:58.950 --> 00:05:02.330
And then bring him back here, 
on top of it all! Why?

00:05:02.330 --> 00:05:05.680
How much are you trying to embarrass me?

00:05:05.680 --> 00:05:09.120
Yoshida-san came here for me.

00:05:09.120 --> 00:05:10.970
For you?

00:05:10.970 --> 00:05:14.540
You're not part of this family! 
This isn't your problem!

00:05:14.540 --> 00:05:16.220
Mother, that's rude.

00:05:16.220 --> 00:05:17.580
Issa, shut up!

00:05:18.360 --> 00:05:20.320
What does "taking care of you" mean, anyway?

00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:23.440
He was just letting a teenage girl 
stay in his house, right?

00:05:23.440 --> 00:05:24.190
Mom!

00:05:24.190 --> 00:05:26.710
I said, "Shut up!"

00:05:28.040 --> 00:05:29.690
You're right.

00:05:31.650 --> 00:05:39.060
I let Sayu stay in my home, 
even when I knew it was against the law.

00:05:40.660 --> 00:05:43.290
Why did you bring him here?

00:05:43.290 --> 00:05:44.490
Because...

00:05:44.490 --> 00:05:48.280
It doesn't become okay just because 
you know it's against the law!

00:05:48.670 --> 00:05:50.730
It just makes you a criminal!

00:05:54.900 --> 00:05:56.620
Every single time...

00:05:58.210 --> 00:06:02.810
Every single time you treat the people 
I care about as if they don't matter!

00:06:02.810 --> 00:06:04.880
You insult them without
even listening to them!

00:06:04.880 --> 00:06:07.220
That's what I hate about you!

00:06:15.240 --> 00:06:20.440
Yoshida-san took good care of me.

00:06:21.640 --> 00:06:25.020
When I ran away from home... 
and ran even further...

00:06:27.430 --> 00:06:30.180
I told myself that I needed 
to put up with painful things,

00:06:30.770 --> 00:06:33.130
so I could get away from the real pain.

00:06:33.730 --> 00:06:35.370
Every single day I told myself that.

00:06:36.600 --> 00:06:42.120
But the truth is, 
I hated what I was doing so much!

00:06:45.140 --> 00:06:48.640
Yoshida-san told me 
what I was doing was wrong.

00:06:48.640 --> 00:06:52.280
And then he accepted me for who I was. 
Told me I could stay with him.

00:06:52.820 --> 00:06:56.040
And gave me a place 
I could be happy to call home.

00:07:02.110 --> 00:07:06.980
Yoshida-san saw me as a person.

00:07:07.780 --> 00:07:11.360
He treated me like family! 
Not like you!

00:07:14.870 --> 00:07:16.980
What are you talking about?

00:07:21.000 --> 00:07:22.740
You don't....!

00:07:22.740 --> 00:07:23.900
Understand...!

00:07:24.320 --> 00:07:25.960
How hard it is for me!

00:07:29.120 --> 00:07:34.380
How much I lost because of you!

00:07:35.810 --> 00:07:40.060
Really, I should've never given birth to you!

00:08:05.240 --> 00:08:06.410
<i>No...</i>

00:08:07.140 --> 00:08:09.260
<i>What I should do right now is...</i>

00:08:33.780 --> 00:08:35.990
That's enough.

00:08:51.440 --> 00:08:53.010
<i>It feels strange.</i>

00:08:54.130 --> 00:09:00.070
<i>I almost threw the glass in her face, 
but I held back.</i>

00:09:00.720 --> 00:09:05.480
<i>And then I realized there were 
two different feelings mixed up inside me.</i>

00:09:06.770 --> 00:09:09.600
<i>One I felt boiling up 
from deep inside my belly,</i>

00:09:09.600 --> 00:09:13.620
<i>and a quiet feeling 
pushing down on it from above.</i>

00:09:14.960 --> 00:09:19.000
<i>I'm simultaneously infuriated and calm.</i>

00:09:23.810 --> 00:09:26.470
<i>Nobody chooses to be born.</i>

00:09:26.930 --> 00:09:29.400
<i>A mother and father are bound together,</i>

00:09:29.400 --> 00:09:33.240
<i>and then the child is born 
whether they want to be or not.</i>

00:09:33.960 --> 00:09:40.250
<i>But is a child responsible 
for their own life?</i>

00:09:41.400 --> 00:09:44.410
<i>I think the answer is no.</i>

00:09:46.230 --> 00:09:54.990
<i>People truly become able to be responsible 
for themselves only after they grow up.</i>

00:09:55.570 --> 00:10:02.950
<i>That's not a burden that a child 
whose mind hasn't fully matured can bear.</i>

00:10:04.040 --> 00:10:11.880
<i>But Sayu never realized that,
and she struggled... and struggled...</i>

00:10:14.600 --> 00:10:16.800
<i>And suffered so much.</i>

00:10:18.150 --> 00:10:21.160
<i>My job now is...</i>

00:10:26.120 --> 00:10:28.760
If a parent doesn't have the ability 
to choose their children,

00:10:28.760 --> 00:10:31.430
a child doesn't have the ability 
to choose their parents, either.

00:10:32.720 --> 00:10:37.940
The only person who will
ever be her mother is you.

00:10:39.410 --> 00:10:43.910
A child doesn't know how to survive 
without their parents.

00:10:45.760 --> 00:10:49.030
If you really don't care about Sayu,

00:10:51.430 --> 00:10:54.090
I'd like to take her in myself.

00:10:55.320 --> 00:11:00.800
I want to raise her up until she's an adult.

00:11:02.500 --> 00:11:05.800
But... But I can't do that.

00:11:06.240 --> 00:11:08.640
That's not how it works!

00:11:10.750 --> 00:11:13.690
It's not my responsibility.

00:11:13.690 --> 00:11:16.320
I don't have the responsibility, 
so I don't have the right.

00:11:16.910 --> 00:11:19.000
If something happens to her,

00:11:19.000 --> 00:11:24.030
helping her, and taking responsibility
for her, is her family's job.

00:11:24.520 --> 00:11:28.340
That responsibility creates a duty.

00:11:28.740 --> 00:11:31.250
And gives weight to the things you do.

00:11:33.920 --> 00:11:35.100
But...

00:11:37.240 --> 00:11:41.200
I don't have any of those things.

00:11:41.200 --> 00:11:45.890
I can't truly protect her when it matters.

00:11:46.870 --> 00:11:48.470
It has to be you!

00:11:50.320 --> 00:11:54.900
Nobody has the right to raise her but you.

00:11:56.730 --> 00:11:57.770
So...

00:12:20.680 --> 00:12:26.340
Please, raise Sayu until she can stand 
on her own two feet.

00:12:27.000 --> 00:12:28.430
I beg you.

00:12:30.020 --> 00:12:31.770
Yoshida-san, no...

00:12:33.700 --> 00:12:37.800
Why would a total stranger do this?

00:12:45.920 --> 00:12:50.170
I'm asking you, too, Mother.

00:12:54.080 --> 00:12:55.610
You too, Issa?

00:13:02.480 --> 00:13:04.540
Wh-What?

00:13:04.540 --> 00:13:05.590
What the hell is going on?!

00:13:12.230 --> 00:13:15.660
Get out! Get out!

00:13:16.600 --> 00:13:17.820
Mom!

00:13:17.820 --> 00:13:19.290
What the hell is this?

00:13:19.810 --> 00:13:21.610
What the hell is wrong with you?

00:13:21.610 --> 00:13:22.940
I'm sorry.

00:13:22.940 --> 00:13:24.570
Would you please leave for now.

00:13:24.570 --> 00:13:26.250
I'll take care of things.

00:13:26.250 --> 00:13:27.250
All right.

00:13:28.530 --> 00:13:29.920
You too, Sayu.

00:13:29.920 --> 00:13:31.830
O-Okay...

00:13:31.830 --> 00:13:34.080
Get out now!

00:13:34.080 --> 00:13:36.570
It's okay. It's okay now.

00:13:39.210 --> 00:13:41.040
What the hell is this?

00:13:58.150 --> 00:14:00.360
What's wrong, Yoshida-san?

00:14:00.360 --> 00:14:02.070
Why are you crying?

00:14:06.080 --> 00:14:09.030
When I heard your story,

00:14:10.590 --> 00:14:17.750
I thought I understood 
how your mother felt about you.

00:14:18.720 --> 00:14:19.800
But...

00:14:20.550 --> 00:14:24.600
when she said she never
should've given birth to you,

00:14:24.600 --> 00:14:29.080
I realized it was far,
far worse than I thought.

00:14:30.760 --> 00:14:33.720
I couldn't take it.

00:14:33.720 --> 00:14:35.980
I-It's okay, Yoshida-san!

00:14:35.980 --> 00:14:37.230
It's not okay!

00:14:40.540 --> 00:14:45.230
Get mad. Say something to her!

00:14:48.260 --> 00:14:52.440
Yoshida-san, I was about to get mad, too.

00:14:54.020 --> 00:14:55.020
But...

00:14:57.200 --> 00:15:00.280
You got mad first.

00:15:07.110 --> 00:15:11.080
Thank you, Yoshida-san.

00:15:36.660 --> 00:15:39.290
It's so beautiful 
that it almost doesn't seem fair.

00:15:39.290 --> 00:15:40.890
The night sky.

00:15:40.890 --> 00:15:41.900
Right?

00:15:46.110 --> 00:15:48.280
Um, Yoshida-san.

00:15:50.290 --> 00:15:56.430
When you got on your knees in front of her, 
I felt as if I'd been forgiven.

00:15:58.370 --> 00:16:02.410
I did so many things that were wrong.

00:16:03.640 --> 00:16:05.880
But it wasn't all for nothing.

00:16:11.270 --> 00:16:12.680
It's okay.

00:16:13.830 --> 00:16:17.830
Even without you, I can stand on my own.

00:16:19.940 --> 00:16:22.000
So don't worry.

00:16:30.820 --> 00:16:31.690
Okay.

00:16:37.780 --> 00:16:39.140
Do your best.

00:16:47.120 --> 00:16:47.800
Yeah.

00:16:56.790 --> 00:17:02.410
<i>From the perspective of other people, 
the whole world, the universe...</i>

00:17:03.000 --> 00:17:07.700
<i>The bigger the scale you look at, 
the smaller we are...</i>

00:17:08.320 --> 00:17:09.430
<i>But by chance,</i>

00:17:10.420 --> 00:17:15.240
<i>the path Sayu crossed 
intersected with my own,</i>

00:17:15.240 --> 00:17:17.370
<i>and I became a part of her history.</i>

00:17:18.280 --> 00:17:22.720
<i>Will the day come 
when she remembers this?</i>

00:17:24.280 --> 00:17:31.020
<i>And when that day comes, 
will she have grown up?</i>

00:17:40.060 --> 00:17:42.060
You're very close, huh?

00:17:45.000 --> 00:17:47.160
We settled things.

00:17:47.670 --> 00:17:49.690
H-How did it go?

00:17:49.690 --> 00:17:54.250
For now, you need to stay here 
until you graduate.

00:17:54.250 --> 00:18:00.640
Mother says that as long as you don't
cause any problems, she won't bother you.

00:18:02.420 --> 00:18:04.220
But that's...

00:18:04.220 --> 00:18:08.940
Of course, those were just words. 
We don't know it'll actually go like that.

00:18:09.380 --> 00:18:15.480
But Yoshida-san's words seem 
to have affected her, a little.

00:18:16.480 --> 00:18:21.350
And Sayu came back a little more grown-up.

00:18:21.860 --> 00:18:26.790
It might be time for the two of them 
to figure out how to get along together.

00:18:27.600 --> 00:18:31.030
Of course, I'll help.

00:18:33.400 --> 00:18:36.170
Yeah. That's right.

00:18:36.780 --> 00:18:40.410
Things with Mom aren't going 
to get better quickly.

00:18:40.850 --> 00:18:45.030
But I can try to make them better.

00:18:46.580 --> 00:18:49.290
I'd always given up on it.

00:18:55.840 --> 00:19:01.110
I was worried for a moment. 
I guess it's all settled for now.

00:19:03.220 --> 00:19:05.000
It's thanks to you, Yoshida-san.

00:19:05.450 --> 00:19:08.480
No, I didn't...

00:19:08.480 --> 00:19:11.780
I just said what I was feeling.

00:19:13.970 --> 00:19:18.260
A grown-up shouldn't behave 
the way I did.

00:19:20.130 --> 00:19:25.840
No, the fact that you got 
on your knees convinced her.

00:19:25.840 --> 00:19:28.220
If anything, it's a little frustrating.

00:19:28.220 --> 00:19:30.140
Frustrating?

00:19:30.140 --> 00:19:32.850
Yes. I'm Sayu's brother,

00:19:33.430 --> 00:19:37.020
and I never got on my knees for her.

00:19:37.540 --> 00:19:39.110
But you...

00:19:40.490 --> 00:19:45.070
You were able to do it. And mean it.

00:19:46.880 --> 00:19:50.100
I couldn't do that.

00:19:51.280 --> 00:19:52.870
No...

00:19:54.880 --> 00:19:56.470
Thank you, really.

00:19:58.630 --> 00:19:59.500
Yeah.

00:19:59.910 --> 00:20:03.600
Yoshida-san, it's late.

00:20:03.600 --> 00:20:05.580
Stay here tonight.

00:20:09.220 --> 00:20:14.650
Um... May I speak to your mother again?

00:20:21.990 --> 00:20:23.240
All right.

00:20:24.040 --> 00:20:25.400
Thank you.

00:20:37.760 --> 00:20:40.300
Sayu, can you give me a little time?

00:20:43.380 --> 00:20:44.360
Sure.

00:20:49.750 --> 00:20:52.500
I'm very sorry about what I just did.

00:20:52.930 --> 00:20:56.650
I lost control and said things 
I shouldn't have said.

00:20:56.650 --> 00:21:02.610
It's too late for that. 
You already barged into a stranger's house.

00:21:04.080 --> 00:21:07.820
You really didn't do anything with Sayu?

00:21:08.280 --> 00:21:10.790
I didn't. I swear.

00:21:12.920 --> 00:21:16.940
Then why are you doing all this for her?

00:21:18.440 --> 00:21:23.320
Because I met her on that day, 
in that moment.

00:21:27.310 --> 00:21:28.520
That's the only reason.

00:21:30.790 --> 00:21:31.740
I see.

00:21:32.560 --> 00:21:34.860
Um, Sayu...

00:21:34.860 --> 00:21:41.990
I'm going to think about
our future after we talk.

00:21:45.420 --> 00:21:50.490
So go back to Tokyo in the morning.

00:21:54.980 --> 00:21:58.120
Yes. I will.

00:23:29.920 --> 00:23:34.930
<b>Next Time</b>

00:23:29.920 --> 00:23:34.930
"Future"

00:23:34.930 --> 00:23:39.930
<b>Watch next week. I'm begging you.</b>
